WEBVTT

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.660
The story until now.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.450
The results from my checkup at a hospital in Musashino were grim.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.980
I have 62 years left to live.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.200
This fact was very difficult for me to accept.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.710
Had I known earlier, I would've left politics and made mistakes

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.310
like becoming a host, or a prostitute, or a drug addict.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.370
Had I done that, I would've been more popular with the youth while maintaining this disease.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.020
I looked up at the white ceiling and screamed.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.590
I screamed at the Gods,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.460
“I hate this cruel fate you've bestowed upon me!”

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.760
“A disgraceful atheist such as yourself
shouldn't be complaining to them at all,”

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.080
replied a nurse that entered the room from behind the curtain.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.330
“Since you're in here, is there a
specific God you wish to worship?”

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.230
Ah, of course she would introduce Gods to me, since she's an angel in white!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.910
“Are there any Gods you'd recommend?”

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.220
“Sure, I'll give you my recommendations in exchange for all of your assets...”

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.150
Just then, another nurse entered the room.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.880
“Hold it. I know Gods that are much better than any of the ones she can recommend.”

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.280
Ah, of course this nurse would introduce better Gods to me, since she's an angel in white!

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.600
“In dialectical materialism, you'll find an opportunity in death,” she replied.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.410
Then, an unexpected third nurse entered the room...

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.600
I think it's better if you don't open it.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:55.760
If you don't open it, the possibility of you receiving and not receiving chocolate will exist.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.130
Thus, creating a multiverse.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.810
Schrödinger's cat.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.790
It follows the same principle.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.230
Sch-Schrö... who?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:12.290
I'll spare you the technicalities.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.930
Basically, you put a cat that might die in a box.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.730
If you don't open the box, the possibility of the cat

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.430
being alive and dead will simultaneously exist.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.390
In other words, as long as I don't open my locker,

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.450
there's still a possibility that I got chocolate, right?!

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.480
I got chocolate!

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.770
There's no way in Hell I'll ever open this again!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.570
Aside from putting chocolate in lockers in this day and age,

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.940
there are plenty of happy endings that come from opening boxes.

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.330
And you'll never know if you don't open it.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:51.660
But if you don't, the possibilities remain infinite!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.410
It's Schrödinger's forehead.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.170
Forehead?

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.560
Back in the day, when I thought my hairline was receding,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.420
I put this box on my head to cover it.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:06.300
As long as I don't remove it, there's both the possibility that I have hair and that I'm bald!

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.960
That's right!

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.080
In another universe, you still have a full head of hair!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.480
I guess that's true...

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.690
Your hairline's already receding, so 
covering it up now is somewhat pointless.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.910
So.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:26.120
I'd like for everybody to use Schrödinger's experiment and apply it to yourselves.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.760
Schrö...?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.770
It sounds kinda complicated...

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.270
Nami, did you get fatter?

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.720
I did not!

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.000
Denied that quickly.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.170
For Ms. Hito,

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.720
I give you Schrödinger's scale.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.150
As long as you don't remove the box,

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:50.850
the possibility of you gaining and not gaining weight exist simultaneously.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.630
You're lucky.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.370
You have infinite possibilities.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.040
Are you messing with me?!

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.250
And for Ms. Kobushi,

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.780
I give you Schrödinger's tail.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.070
As long as I don't open this box,

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:09.490
there's infinite possibilities for tails!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.370
In a multiverse, all kind of tails can exist!

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.340
Oh, I...

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.550
Brought this here last week...

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.820
And left it in my desk.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:26.840
I haven't eaten it yet either...

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.990
Is this...

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.800
It's Schrödinger's lunch box.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:35.340
As long as you don't open it, there's the possibility that the contents are edible,

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:39.420
and there's the possibility that new life was born from the contents.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.400
Oh, Mr. Assemblyman.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.490
It's Schrödinger's ballot box.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.720
As long as this box isn't opened,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.510
there's still the possibility that you can remain in office!

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.200
You can't bring the ballot box here!

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:57.250
In any case, as long as the box isn't opened, there are infinite possibilities!

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.180
Schrödinger's Boyfriend's Cell phone
Schrödinger's Make-Up
Schrödinger's Bra
Schrödinger's Refrigerator
Schrödinger's Vintage Wine
Schrödinger's Porngraphic Vending Machine
Schrödinger's First Choice Baseball Draft
Schrödinger's Legal Counsel
Schrödinger's Mail Certification
Schrödinger's Radiography
Schrödinger's Hot Spring
Schrödinger's Oil Field (Commercial Scam)
Schrödinger's Breaching Submarine
Schrödinger's Single Room for the Elderly
Schrödinger's Dead Sea Scrolls
Schrödinger's Popular Questionnaire

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.790
I hate to interrupt, but I thought I'd
congratulate Kei on his second marriage.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.690
I didn't know he divorced Yuka...

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:04.920
The stain on the wall.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.410
This is my new wife.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.930
It's Schrödinger's wife.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:17.640
As long as the box isn't opened, I can continue having multiple possibilities for my ideal wife!

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.900
I wonder what she looks like inside.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.020
I want to know too!

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.260
Whoops, the chisel slipped out of my hand!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.050
She's hairy!

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.390
Unthinkable!

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.990
My ideal wife's possibilities have reduced a little!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.120
You call that a little?

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.640
Whoops, they slipped out of my hand again!

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:42.040
She's got beautiful legs!

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.660
No! My ideal wife's image is becoming warped!

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.760
Brother, what kind of image were you hoping for?!

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.730
I don't think humanity is prepared to see your wife!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.660
Teacher, why don't you choose one of Schrödinger's wives?

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.230
Pick whoever you like.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.680
They're all boxed-in girls, of course.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.550
You don't have to make puns!

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:21.050
As long as you don't open them up, there's the possibility that you have a loyal wife!

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:24.940
I think I'll know who's inside which box without opening them.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.150
That box is telling you to choose it.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.080
But I don't want this one!

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.070
What?!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.390
How about I stuff you inside a box?!

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.550
It's Schrödinger's teacher!

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:45.650
Infinite variations of our teacher exist inside the box!

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.420
Then,

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.080
there's the possibility of there being two of them in the same box, right?!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.020
The students in this class are truly an inspiration.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.990
They can be anything!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.330
That's right.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.110
As long as they remain closed, the possibilities for all students become infinite!

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.370
Infinite possibilities...?

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.010
Then that means

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:18.640
the possibility of someone existing only to tease, badmouth, and insult me is infinite.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.720
Unforgivable!

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.000
Why's the door closed?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.860
It's Schrödinger's classroom.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.260
As long as we don't open it,

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:34.070
there's the possibility that every student will attend class without incident!

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:34.240
Planning

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:34.410
Staff

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:34.570
Budget

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:34.740
Schedule

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:34.910
Quality

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:35.160
Quantity sold

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.030
What are you doing?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.230
I've got a feeling that the third season of this anime won't air.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.650
So, as long as I don't open that box,

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:52.200
there's both the possibility of the third season airing and not airing.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.930
Of course they're going to air it, you wuss!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.970
Fabulously delish!

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:07.890
What'll we do?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.640
What should we do?

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.030
Quite the quandary.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:15.230
The satellite

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:15.400
couldn't

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:15.560
take off, right?

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:15.730
They

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:15.900
couldn't

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:16.150
hear anything.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.850
This is <i>it</i>, right?

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.230
The one in the news.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:28.320
The missil—

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.160
Don't say such reckless things!

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.870
The news said that it passed over the archipelago.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:36.990
So, the JSDF failed to intercept the missile and it fell?

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.750
N-No way...

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.300
Then what are we looking at?

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.930
For now, we should contact the authorities.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.410
Wait a second!

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:52.410
The missile wasn't destroyed and nobody's reported it yet.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:55.180
This is definitely a national secret, right?!

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:58.480
The government will probably do
everything possible to keep this a secret!

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.860
And now that we know their secret, they're gonna make us disappear.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:03.850
Th— {line added - el}

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.400
That can't be...

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:14.400
I-I know!

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:19.880
We should tell this to the media outlets, so the government can't do a thing!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:22.900
The media...

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.150
You think they're reliable?

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:30.720
Besides, this missile fell and it still hasn't been reported yet.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.010
I didn't see a thing.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.440
Me neither.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.560
I saw nothing.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:39.060
Hold it!

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:42.440
You can't try ignoring something as dangerous as this!

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.360
If we do nothing about it,

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.110
this could very well end with a bang!

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.530
You're absolutely right!

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.970
We've ended with too many bangs already!

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.370
We haven't had one recently, so it's okay if we do this time, right?

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.350
On a side note, I have some great news.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:02.840
A news outlet is coming today to interview our baseball team.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.450
Why now of all times?!

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.920
Apparently, one of the freshmen is an incredible pitcher.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.740
They'll rat us out when they find out!

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.220
We have to fool them somehow!

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:18.270
Doesn't it resemble a decoration from an athletics festival?

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:20.380
You're right!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.780
We'll pretend that it's a decoration from an athletics festival.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:28.550
It'll look more convincing after I finish writing this sporty slogan.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.220
You've basically confirmed that it's a missile.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.540
But it's a sporty slogan they use at most athletic festivals.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.950
We have to do better than this if we want to fool the reporters.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:46.000
C'mon people, think!{check timing - probably in wrong place}

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:52.340
Why don't we just flat-out deny it being a missile by writing “Fake” on it?

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.930
Now it looks legitimate.

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:58.100
Indeed.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.090
I don't get it!

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.560
Why would you say that?

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:02.750
You don't get it?

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:06.770
For instance, how would these bank
notes look to you if they said “Fake”?

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:09.150
They'd look legitimate!

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.300
It's the same principle.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:12.350
So, what's our next move?

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.280
Let's just bury it.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:20.950
I-It sticks out like a sore thumb now.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.920
You can tell that something is buried under there.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:28.160
There's got to be a way to make it look natural.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.420
I have an idea.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.880
We'll think of this as

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.020
a natural mound.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.350
My goodness, it does look natural now.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.040
Eh?

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.890
They're coming to interview the baseball team, so it's convenient!

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:43.600
Wait a minute!

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.690
You can't call <i>this</i> a mound!

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:46.980
I guess not...

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.110
The baseball diamond has to be there in order for a mound to exist.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:50.360
You meant that?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.870
All right. I'll draw the lines around the mound.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.740
The chalk isn't coming out evenly.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:13:00.290
Hey, the line's going to overlap into the tennis court.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:02.490
Emergencies like this take priority.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:03.830
We'll apologize later.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.170
Brother, there's a problem.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:15.370
Instead of concealing it, you've just
determined which country launched it.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.280
Are you kidding me?!

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.890
Forget hiding it! What would happen if a satellite were to take a photo of this?!

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:23.160
The mound is rejected!

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.890
We have to think of another method!

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.690
It collapsed!

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:31.190
We don't have any time left to bury it again!

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.360
I know.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.670
This must be a...

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.240
Time capsule!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.720
Graduate students buried it ages ago, and it resurfaced due to diastrophism!

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.000
Are you deluding yourself?

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.290
It's a cassette tape.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:53.120
I was right! It is a time capsule!

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.930
There're probably a few classics on it!

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.320
Try putting it in.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:59.010
This came with it.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:02.600
So SONY used to be SONV?

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.120
Oh, they're singing.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.110
But the quality's so bad that I can't make out the lyrics too well.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.760
Don't you find this tune moving?

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:13.310
I do.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:18.020
It sounds like they're praising a wonderful person.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.200
Let's pump up the volume!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:26.610
What's going on?

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:30.390
We're having a festival which celebrates age-old local traditions that encourages national prestige.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.770
And this object is the embodiment of our local deity!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.240
Come everyone, let's all participate in the festivity!

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:40.610
In the promised land lies the flying object.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:44.470
Bombarding the Earth paradise.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.460
Teacher!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:49.090
You don't have to lie to them anymore!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:52.320
That missile really was a fake!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.570
Because the real one is over there!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:13.940
So this still ends with a baaang!

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:21.510
On

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:21.680
time

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:21.840
un

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:22.010
in

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:22.220
ten

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:22.470
tionally.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.290
Ra-men! Ra-men!

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.290
Is she okay?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.010
I don't know.

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:42.080
The ramen joint is on the other side of this wall.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.260
All right!

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.240
Finally, we've made it!

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:49.770
Naturally, I've purchased this restaurant as well.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.960
Rub a dub dub, thanks for the grub!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:02.780
The owner changed, so the flavor changed...

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:06.720
You're the new owner, Milady.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:07.780
I never saw it coming.

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:10.270
You think you can blow this off with a cheap laugh?!

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.230
Now I'm disappointed.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:16.080
Let's go to a karaoke box to cheer up!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:16.920
A karaoke box?

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:21.480
If we purchase these properties, we can get there.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.540
You're a high-maintenance classmate.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:31.820
This is getting to be like the escape tunnels the Medicis built in Firenze!

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.520
Wait, why are you guys here?

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:38.050
Our houses were en route.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:42.170
Your beloved karaoke box is beyond this wall.

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:44.220
Come on, karaoke!

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:50.710
Brother!

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:51.430
Rin?!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.420
You were forbidden to go outside!

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.170
Speak for yourself.

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:57.680
By purchasing these properties,

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:02.930
Milady has managed to arrive here without leaving her estate.

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.660
How forceful...

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.890
But I'm safe too.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.500
My legal address can't be at the school.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.170
Officially, I live with Rin.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.190
You all have to get home though.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:18.130
We're fine.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:22.210
Officially, we're members of your household, teacher.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:23.880
But on an unofficial level.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:29.960
Anyway, this way, we can go anywhere without breaking the curfew.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.910
I want to go to the sweets shop!

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.700
You bought the school too?

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.780
Yes. It was en route.

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:47.180
All right class, let's begin.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.660
This is horrible.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.660
This way, even if we're under curfew, we can come to class.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:58.260
I sold the land I bought for that road plan for twice what I paid.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.880
Isn't that just speculation?

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:38.750
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.940
Let's draw using skills befitting of a general.

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:48.750
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:55.370
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:56.820
Lightning...

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:58.500
Flash!

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.010
Lightning...

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.690
Flash!

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:04.990
The rain comes pouring down.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.130
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:11.340
Two puddles were made.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:14.550
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:18.930
We made a fish cake with the fish we caught.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:22.750
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:25.290
Did everyone draw well?

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.480
Bye bye!

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.110
Yanyan teaching step by step.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:37.850
Yanyan let's study.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:41.580
Periods one and two are full of bad boys.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:44.950
But period three has only naughty ones.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:48.060
The boys have been waiting all night for me.

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:51.730
So repeat after me, 2.2360679.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:57.830
For tonight's lesson,

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:01.400
I'll be quizzing you on

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.340
your serious way of life.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.580
Yin, Zhou, and Qin followed perfection,

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:10.800
while Sui, Tang, and Song followed dignity.

00:21:11.210 --> 00:21:14.090
I won't ask for too much,

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:17.850
so don't push it, boys.

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:23.520
On page 108,

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:29.930
recite and praise the great Earthly passions!

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:36.610
We'll swim around the textbook together.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:43.310
The meeting between music and intellect

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:49.690
becomes a match made in heaven.

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:54.550
They'll leave their mark in history.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:58.220
Private Lesson!

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:02.870
Naughty Ms. Kaere!

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:09.160
My answer was wrong.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.000
What?

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:21.220
My answer for the cone's volume from last week

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.680
was wrong.

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:28.810
Because the cones obviously grew more since last week.

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:31.820
Please let me remeasure them!

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:33.570
Noooo!{please check timing}

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:35.970
That's a no-no.{please check timing}

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:38.950
We're not covering the volume of cones today.

00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:42.780
Today, we'll learn how to find a cylinder's volume.

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:48.670
Sorry, you can't get an image just from a diagram.

00:22:48.670 --> 00:22:52.230
I wonder if there's a cylindrical object somewhere.

00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:55.420
Blackout!

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:58.430
Oh, I found a cylinder.

00:22:58.430 --> 00:23:02.890
That's not a very good cylinder, teacher!

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:06.410
The size will keep changing!

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:16.940
In order to learn about the habitats of sea anemones, Ms. Kaere took me to the beach today.

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:20.160
However, we encountered the environmental protection group, Zreenpeace.

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:24.620
They pressured Ms. Kaere to wear something smaller since she was wearing petroleum products.

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:26.730
Next time on Naughty Ms. Kaere:

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:32.190
Lesson 119. Greener Swimsuits Will Save the Earth.

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.920
How about we bury these balls?
